{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"af5a7ada0a231ea00","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01X3wPzW6etqBkGyZBdmjptW","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-ZSaIwY-translated-rust/69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc/tasks/af5a7ada0a231ea00.output","summary":"Done. `src/pcre2_extuni.rs` is a complete transliteration of `c_src/src/pcre2_extuni.c`.\n\nFunctions defined (one, matching the C file's single kept function since `SUPPORT_UNICODE` is defined, so the dummy `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` variant is omitted):\n\n- `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _pcre2_extuni_8(c: u32, eptr: PCRE2_SPTR, start_subject: PCRE2_SPTR, end_subject: PCRE2_SPTR, utf: BOOL, xcount: *mut c_int) -> PCRE2_SPTR` — exported symbol confirmed present in the built `.so` (`T _pcre2_extuni_8`).\n\nFidelity notes:\n- Identical test order: gbtable bit test first (`break`), then the ZWJ/Extended_Pictographic rule, then the Regional Indicator even-count scan, then `was_ep_ZWJ` assignment, then the \"Extend after Extended_Pictographic does not update lgb\" rule, then `eptr += len` and `*xcount += 1`.\n- `lgb`/`rgb`/`len`/`ricount` are `c_int` like C; `ucp_gb*` constants cast with `as c_int`. Table read is via raw pointer (`*_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8.as_ptr().add(lgb as usize)`) to avoid any bounds-check panic, with the same `& (1u32 << rgb)` arithmetic.\n- The RI inner scan uses a plain `break` (inner loop) and `break 'outer` for the `(ricount & 1) != 0` grapheme-break case, so the C `break` targets are preserved exactly. `bptr` starts at `eptr.sub(1)` with `BACKCHAR!` only when `utf`, and the loop condition remains `bptr > start_subject` with the pre-decrement inside.\n- No bug fixes, no reordering, C comments retained.\n\nFinal verification command output:\n\n```\n$ cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/translated_rust && cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A12 | head -60\n(no output)\n```\n\nThe whole crate currently builds clean (`Finished \\`release\\` profile`); only warnings remain, none of which are errors in my file. No other files were modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":34415,"tool_uses":12,"duration_ms":81752},"uuid":"68c6469f-b13b-45f5-8371-569631463276","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc"}
