{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KDUbizjAhAWMkF3qhQyE2Z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Translated from c_src/src/pcre2_error.c\n2\tuse crate::internal::*;\n3\t\n4\t/* The texts of compile-time error messages. Compile-time error numbers start\n5\tat COMPILE_ERROR_BASE (100).\n6\t\n7\tThis used to be a table of strings, but in order to reduce the number of\n8\trelocations needed when a shared library is loaded dynamically, it is now one\n9\tlong string. We cannot use a table of offsets, because the lengths of inserts\n10\tsuch as XSTRING(MAX_NAME_SIZE) are not known. Instead,\n11\tpcre2_get_error_message() counts through to the one it wants - this isn't a\n12\tperformance issue because these strings are used only when there is an error.\n13\t\n14\tEach substring ends with \\0 to insert a null character. This includes the final\n15\tsubstring, so that the whole string ends with \\0\\0, which can be detected when\n16\tcounting through. */\n17\t\n18\tconst COMPILE_ERROR_TEXTS: &[u8] = concat!(\n19\t    \"no error\\0\",\n20\t    \"\\\\ at end of pattern\\0\",\n21\t    \"\\\\c at end of pattern\\0\",\n22\t    \"unrecognized character follows \\\\\\0\",\n23\t    \"numbers out of order in {} quantifier\\0\",\n24\t    /* 5 */\n25\t    \"number too big in {} quantifier\\0\",\n26\t    \"missing terminating ] for character class\\0\",\n27\t    \"escape sequence is invalid in character class\\0\",\n28\t    \"range out of order in character class\\0\",\n29\t    \"quantifier does not follow a repeatable item\\0\",\n30\t    /* 10 */\n31\t    \"internal error: unexpected repeat\\0\",\n32\t    \"unrecognized character after (? or (?-\\0\",\n33\t    \"POSIX named classes are supported only within a class\\0\",\n34\t    \"POSIX collating elements are not supported\\0\",\n35\t    \"missing closing parenthesis\\0\",\n36\t    /* 15 */\n37\t    \"reference to non-existent subpattern\\0\",\n38\t    \"pattern passed as NULL with non-zero length\\0\",\n39\t    \"unrecognised compile-time option bit(s)\\0\",\n40\t    \"missing ) after (?# comment\\0\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JtmcPBB2pwTWBVM8D51ZEn","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc","uuid":"9a7ec0c5-8ae8-4c30-8645-d041d4136bc3","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:15:06.070Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pcre2_error.c"}
