{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"afaf0232f85615e91","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015sJJBrMeDQfph143gufXux","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-ZSaIwY-translated-rust/69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc/tasks/afaf0232f85615e91.output","summary":"All 10 exported symbols are present in the built shared library and the crate builds cleanly.\n\n## What was done\n\nOverwrote `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/translated_rust/src/pcre2_jit_compile.rs` with the non-JIT stub translation of `pcre2_jit_compile.c` + `pcre2_jit_match_inc.h` + `pcre2_jit_misc_inc.h`.\n\nFunctions defined (all `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`, exact signatures as specified):\n\n| Symbol | Behaviour (SUPPORT_JIT undefined) |\n|---|---|\n| `pcre2_jit_compile_8` | full non-JIT check chain (see below) |\n| `pcre2_jit_match_8` | `(*match_data).rc = PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION;` then returns `(*match_data).rc` |\n| `pcre2_jit_free_unused_memory_8` | no-op |\n| `pcre2_jit_stack_create_8` | returns `null_mut()` |\n| `pcre2_jit_stack_assign_8` | no-op |\n| `pcre2_jit_stack_free_8` | no-op |\n| `_pcre2_jit_free_rodata_8` | no-op |\n| `_pcre2_jit_free_8` | no-op |\n| `_pcre2_jit_get_size_8` | returns `0` |\n| `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8` | returns pointer to private `static JIT_TARGET_NOT_SUPPORTED: [u8; 21] = *b\"JIT is not supported\\0\"` |\n\n`pcre2_jit_compile_8` reproduces the C order of tests exactly:\n1. `re = code` cast first (before the NULL check, as in C).\n2. `if options & PCRE2_JIT_TEST_ALLOC != 0` -> `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION` if `options != PCRE2_JIT_TEST_ALLOC`, else `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_UNSUPPORTED` (the `#else` branch).\n3. `code.is_null()` -> `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`.\n4. `options & !PUBLIC_JIT_COMPILE_OPTIONS != 0` -> `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION`, with `const PUBLIC_JIT_COMPILE_OPTIONS: u32 = PCRE2_JIT_COMPLETE | PCRE2_JIT_PARTIAL_SOFT | PCRE2_JIT_PARTIAL_HARD | PCRE2_JIT_INVALID_UTF;`.\n5. Side effect preserved: if `PCRE2_JIT_INVALID_UTF` is set and `(*re).overall_options & PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF == 0`, sets `(*re).overall_options |= PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` (the `functions != NULL` early-return is JIT-only and omitted).\n6. Falls through to `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION`.\n\nNote: `internal.rs` already `extern \"C\"`-declares `pcre2_jit_compile_8`, `pcre2_jit_match_8`, `_pcre2_jit_free_rodata_8`, `_pcre2_jit_free_8`, `_pcre2_jit_get_size_8`, `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8`; the local definitions shadow the glob-imported names without conflict, and the linker resolves the declarations to these definitions. No other file was modified.\n\n## Verification\n\nCommand: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/translated_rust && cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A12 | head -60`\n\nExact output: *(empty — no output at all)*\n\nThe whole crate now builds (`Finished \\`release\\` profile [optimized] target(s)`). An earlier run showed two `E0425` errors in `src/pcre2_error.rs` (another agent's module, since fixed); at no point did any error or warning reference `src/pcre2_jit_compile.rs`.","usage":{"total_tokens":44787,"tool_uses":17,"duration_ms":109472},"uuid":"9b16bcc4-2a3c-4681-8eb1-119c794f0566","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kbpzn5huneuiq2bcc4pzekyeuu4cnxi6cowtmtv27mfdzsk3s6tq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01U6KGaodczzWgaY2hrWFS7e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/translated_rust/src/pcre2_pattern_info.rs","content":"// Translated from c_src/src/pcre2_pattern_info.c\nuse crate::internal::*;\n\n/* The code unit width of this library; used for the mode check below, exactly\nas the C macro PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH does. */\n\nconst PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH: u32 = 8;\n\n/*************************************************\n*        Return info about compiled pattern      *\n*************************************************/\n\n/*\nArguments:\n  code          points to compiled code\n  what          what information is required\n  where         where to put the information; if NULL, return length\n\nReturns:        0 when data returned\n                > 0 when length requested\n                < 0 on error or unset value\n*/\n\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn pcre2_pattern_info_8(\n    code: *const pcre2_real_code,\n    what: u32,\n    where_: *mut c_void,\n) -> c_int {\n    let re: *const pcre2_real_code = code;\n\n    if where_.is_null()\n    /* Requests field length */\n    {\n        match what {\n            PCRE2_INFO_ALLOPTIONS\n            | PCRE2_INFO_ARGOPTIONS\n            | PCRE2_INFO_BACKREFMAX\n            | PCRE2_INFO_BSR\n            | PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_DEPTHLIMIT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_EXTRAOPTIONS\n            | PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODETYPE\n            | PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODEUNIT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_HASBACKSLASHC\n            | PCRE2_INFO_HASCRORLF\n            | PCRE2_INFO_HEAPLIMIT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_JCHANGED\n            | PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODETYPE\n            | PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODEUNIT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_MATCHEMPTY\n            | PCRE2_INFO_MATCHLIMIT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_MAXLOOKBEHIND\n            | PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH\n            | PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE\n            | PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT\n            | PCRE2_INFO_NEWLINE => {\n                return size_of::<u32>() as c_int;\n            }\n\n            PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP => {\n                return size_of::<*const u8>() as c_int;\n            }\n\n            PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE | PCRE2_INFO_SIZE | PCRE2_INFO_FRAMESIZE => {\n                return size_of::<usize>() as c_int;\n            }\n\n            PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE => {\n                return size_of::<PCRE2_SPTR>() as c_int;\n            }\n\n            _ => {}\n        }\n    }\n\n    if re.is_null() {\n        return PCRE2_ERROR_NULL;\n    }\n\n    /* Check that the first field in the block is the magic number. If it is not,\n    return with PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC. */\n\n    if (*re).magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER {\n        return PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC;\n    }\n\n    /* Check that this pattern was compiled in the correct bit mode */\n\n    if ((*re).flags & (PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH / 8)) == 0 {\n        return PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE;\n    }\n\n    match what {\n        PCRE2_INFO_ALLOPTIONS => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).overall_options;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_ARGOPTIONS => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).compile_options;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_BACKREFMAX => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).top_backref as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_BSR => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).bsr_convention as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_CAPTURECOUNT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).top_bracket as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_DEPTHLIMIT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).limit_depth;\n            if (*re).limit_depth == u32::MAX {\n                return PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET;\n            }\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_EXTRAOPTIONS => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).extra_options;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODETYPE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = if ((*re).flags & PCRE2_FIRSTSET) != 0 {\n                1\n            } else if ((*re).flags & PCRE2_STARTLINE) != 0 {\n                2\n            } else {\n                0\n            };\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTCODEUNIT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = if ((*re).flags & PCRE2_FIRSTSET) != 0 {\n                (*re).first_codeunit\n            } else {\n                0\n            };\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBITMAP => {\n            *(where_ as *mut *const u8) = if ((*re).flags & PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET) != 0 {\n                (*re).start_bitmap.as_ptr()\n            } else {\n                std::ptr::null()\n            };\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_FRAMESIZE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut usize) = offset_of!(heapframe, ovector)\n                + (*re).top_bracket as usize * 2 * size_of::<PCRE2_SIZE>();\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_HASBACKSLASHC => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (((*re).flags & PCRE2_HASBKC) != 0) as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_HASCRORLF => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (((*re).flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF) != 0) as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_HEAPLIMIT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).limit_heap;\n            if (*re).limit_heap == u32::MAX {\n                return PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET;\n            }\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_JCHANGED => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (((*re).flags & PCRE2_JCHANGED) != 0) as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE => {\n            /* SUPPORT_JIT is not defined */\n            *(where_ as *mut usize) = 0;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODETYPE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = if ((*re).flags & PCRE2_LASTSET) != 0 { 1 } else { 0 };\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_LASTCODEUNIT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = if ((*re).flags & PCRE2_LASTSET) != 0 {\n                (*re).last_codeunit\n            } else {\n                0\n            };\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_MATCHEMPTY => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (((*re).flags & PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY) != 0) as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_MATCHLIMIT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).limit_match;\n            if (*re).limit_match == u32::MAX {\n                return PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET;\n            }\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_MAXLOOKBEHIND => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).max_lookbehind as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).minlength as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMEENTRYSIZE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).name_entry_size as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMECOUNT => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).name_count as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_NAMETABLE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut PCRE2_SPTR) =\n                (re as *const c_char).add(size_of::<pcre2_real_code>()) as PCRE2_SPTR;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_NEWLINE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut u32) = (*re).newline_convention as u32;\n        }\n\n        PCRE2_INFO_SIZE => {\n            *(where_ as *mut usize) = (*re).blocksize;\n        }\n\n        _ => return PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION,\n    }\n\n    0\n}\n\n/*************************************************\n*              Callout enumerator                *\n*************************************************/\n\n/*\nArguments:\n  code          points to compiled code\n  callback      function called for each callout block\n  callout_data  user data passed to the callback\n\nReturns:        0 when successfully completed\n                < 0 on local error\n               != 0 for callback error\n*/\n\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn pcre2_callout_enumerate_8(\n    code: *const pcre2_real_code,\n    callback: pcre2_callout_enumerate_fn,\n    callout_data: *mut c_void,\n) -> c_int {\n    let re: *const pcre2_real_code = code;\n    let mut cb: pcre2_callout_enumerate_block = std::mem::zeroed();\n    let mut cc: PCRE2_SPTR;\n    let utf: BOOL;\n\n    if re.is_null() {\n        return PCRE2_ERROR_NULL;\n    }\n\n    utf = (((*re).overall_options & PCRE2_UTF) != 0) as BOOL;\n\n    /* Check that the first field in the block is the magic number. If it is not,\n    return with PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC. */\n\n    if (*re).magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER {\n        return PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC;\n    }\n\n    /* Check that this pattern was compiled in the correct bit mode */\n\n    if ((*re).flags & (PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH / 8)) == 0 {\n        return PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE;\n    }\n\n    cb.version = 0;\n    cc = (re as *const u8).add((*re).code_start) as PCRE2_SPTR;\n\n    loop {\n        let rc: c_int;\n        match *cc as u32 {\n            OP_END => {\n                return 0;\n            }\n\n            OP_CHAR\n            | OP_CHARI\n            | OP_NOT\n            | OP_NOTI\n            | OP_STAR\n            | OP_MINSTAR\n            | OP_PLUS\n            | OP_MINPLUS\n            | OP_QUERY\n            | OP_MINQUERY\n            | OP_UPTO\n            | OP_MINUPTO\n            | OP_EXACT\n            | OP_POSSTAR\n            | OP_POSPLUS\n            | OP_POSQUERY\n            | OP_POSUPTO\n            | OP_STARI\n            | OP_MINSTARI\n            | OP_PLUSI\n            | OP_MINPLUSI\n            | OP_QUERYI\n            | OP_MINQUERYI\n            | OP_UPTOI\n            | OP_MINUPTOI\n            | OP_EXACTI\n            | OP_POSSTARI\n            | OP_POSPLUSI\n            | OP_POSQUERYI\n            | OP_POSUPTOI\n            | OP_NOTSTAR\n            | OP_NOTMINSTAR\n            | OP_NOTPLUS\n            | OP_NOTMINPLUS\n            | OP_NOTQUERY\n            | OP_NOTMINQUERY\n            | OP_NOTUPTO\n            | OP_NOTMINUPTO\n            | OP_NOTEXACT\n            | OP_NOTPOSSTAR\n            | OP_NOTPOSPLUS\n            | OP_NOTPOSQUERY\n            | OP_NOTPOSUPTO\n            | OP_NOTSTARI\n            | OP_NOTMINSTARI\n            | OP_NOTPLUSI\n            | OP_NOTMINPLUSI\n            | OP_NOTQUERYI\n            | OP_NOTMINQUERYI\n            | OP_NOTUPTOI\n            | OP_NOTMINUPTOI\n            | OP_NOTEXACTI\n            | OP_NOTPOSSTARI\n            | OP_NOTPOSPLUSI\n            | OP_NOTPOSQUERYI\n            | OP_NOTPOSUPTOI => {\n                cc = cc.add(*_pcre2_OP_lengths_8.as_ptr().add(*cc as usize) as usize);\n                if utf != 0 && HAS_EXTRALEN!(*cc.offset(-1)) {\n                    cc = cc.add(GET_EXTRALEN!(*cc.offset(-1)) as usize);\n                }\n            }\n\n            OP_TYPESTAR\n            | OP_TYPEMINSTAR\n            | OP_TYPEPLUS\n            | OP_TYPEMINPLUS\n            | OP_TYPEQUERY\n            | OP_TYPEMINQUERY\n            | OP_TYPEUPTO\n            | OP_TYPEMINUPTO\n            | OP_TYPEEXACT\n            | OP_TYPEPOSSTAR\n            | OP_TYPEPOSPLUS\n            | OP_TYPEPOSQUERY\n            | OP_TYPEPOSUPTO => {\n                cc = cc.add(*_pcre2_OP_lengths_8.as_ptr().add(*cc as usize) as usize);\n                if *cc.offset(-1) as u32 == OP_PROP || *cc.offset(-1) as u32 == OP_NOTPROP {\n                    cc = cc.add(2);\n                }\n            }\n\n            /* SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS */\n            OP_XCLASS | OP_ECLASS => {\n                cc = cc.add(GET!(cc, 1) as usize);\n            }\n\n            OP_MARK | OP_COMMIT_ARG | OP_PRUNE_ARG | OP_SKIP_ARG | OP_THEN_ARG => {\n                cc = cc.add(\n                    *_pcre2_OP_lengths_8.as_ptr().add(*cc as usize) as usize + *cc.add(1) as usize,\n                );\n            }\n\n            OP_CALLOUT => {\n                cb.pattern_position = GET!(cc, 1) as PCRE2_SIZE;\n                cb.next_item_length = GET!(cc, 1 + LINK_SIZE) as PCRE2_SIZE;\n                cb.callout_number = *cc.add(1 + 2 * LINK_SIZE) as u32;\n                cb.callout_string_offset = 0;\n                cb.callout_string_length = 0;\n                cb.callout_string = std::ptr::null();\n                rc = (callback.unwrap())(&mut cb, callout_data);\n                if rc != 0 {\n                    return rc;\n                }\n                cc = cc.add(*_pcre2_OP_lengths_8.as_ptr().add(*cc as usize) as usize);\n            }\n\n            OP_CALLOUT_STR => {\n                cb.pattern_position = GET!(cc, 1) as PCRE2_SIZE;\n                cb.next_item_length = GET!(cc, 1 + LINK_SIZE) as PCRE2_SIZE;\n                cb.callout_number = 0;\n                cb.callout_string_offset = GET!(cc, 1 + 3 * LINK_SIZE) as PCRE2_SIZE;\n                cb.callout_string_length =\n                    (GET!(cc, 1 + 2 * LINK_SIZE) as PCRE2_SIZE) - (1 + 4 * LINK_SIZE) - 2;\n                cb.callout_string = cc.add(1 + 4 * LINK_SIZE).add(1);\n                rc = (callback.unwrap())(&mut cb, callout_data);\n                if rc != 0 {\n                    return rc;\n                }\n                cc = cc.add(GET!(cc, 1 + 2 * LINK_SIZE) as usize);\n            }\n\n            _ => {\n                cc = cc.add(*_pcre2_OP_lengths_8.as_ptr().add(*cc as usize) as usize);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/* End of pcre2_pattern_info.c */\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":43849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":939,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YRFM9xLPzLZZFm6B7W3rPH","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc","uuid":"074c22ac-8415-4f4e-b961-081280a4f3cb","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:16:07.265Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pcre2_pattern_info.c"}
