{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w3xs3nwoerqki4ycczd67t443o25jnybp522u5skmf2ronyyzmnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`src/pcre2_error.rs` is complete and verified.\n\n## What was written\n\n**File:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/translated_rust/src/pcre2_error.rs` (only file touched)\n\n**Function defined (the file's single function, matching the C source):**\n- `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn pcre2_get_error_message_8(enumber: c_int, buffer: *mut PCRE2_UCHAR, size: PCRE2_SIZE) -> c_int` — exact transliteration: same early `size == 0` -> `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, same three-way branch on `COMPILE_ERROR_BASE`/`< 0`/else, same NUL-counting loop returning `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`, same copy loop with `i >= size - 1` truncation setting `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, same unconditional `buffer[i] = 0`, same `rc? rc : (int)i` return. No private helper functions were needed. The EBCDIC on-the-fly translation block is omitted (no EBCDIC).\n\n**Tables** (as `const ... : &[u8] = concat!(...).as_bytes();`, one literal per original C line, with the `/* n */` markers kept as comments):\n- `COMPILE_ERROR_TEXTS`: **121 messages, 5687 bytes total**, ending `\\0\\0`. `XSTRING()` inserts expanded to `8` (UTF-8 mode), `128` (MAX_NAME_SIZE), `10000` (MAX_NAME_COUNT); the non-EBCDIC variant of the `\\c` message kept.\n- `MATCH_ERROR_TEXTS`: **77 messages, 2946 bytes total**, ending `\\0\\0`.\n\nOne correctness detail worth noting: for an invalid error number, C uses the literal `\"\\0\"`, which is **two** bytes (explicit NUL + compiler-added terminator) and the counting loop reads both, so the Rust code uses `b\"\\0\\0\"`; with a 1-byte literal it would read out of bounds.\n\n## Verification performed\n\nRather than hand-typing the tables, I generated them mechanically from the C source (comment/escape/`#ifndef EBCDIC`/`XSTRING` aware), then checked them independently:\n\n1. **Table bytes vs. a real C compiler:** extracted the two table definitions verbatim into a standalone C file, compiled with gcc, dumped the arrays; dumped my Rust consts with a temporary `rustc` binary. `cmp` reports both `compile_error_texts` and `match_error_texts` **byte-identical** (5687 / 2946 bytes, matching `sizeof` from gcc).\n2. **Behaviour vs. a reference C build:** compiled the C function verbatim, `dlopen`ed `target/release/libpcre2.so`, and compared return code *and* the full 300-byte output buffer for every `enumber` in −300..300 across sizes {0,1,2,3,5,10,20,33,64,128,200}: **6611 cases, 0 mismatches** (includes all truncation paths and `size == 0`).\n\n**Exact output of the required verification command** (`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A12 | head -60`): no output — zero errors; the crate links, producing `libpcre2.so`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":57094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":498,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JtmcPBB2pwTWBVM8D51ZEn","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc","uuid":"8b1a2080-983d-4bdd-98aa-97e7dd3359de","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:17:31.958Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pcre2_error.c"}
