{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ETfS7jwHPn6UkdJugNzXT1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PCRE2 C -> Rust translation guide (READ THIS FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tWe are translating the **entire** PCRE2 8-bit library in `c_src/` into a Rust\n4\t`cdylib` that exports the same ABI and produces **byte-identical** behaviour.\n5\t\n6\tBuild config that is already baked in (do not re-derive it):\n7\t`PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 8`, `SUPPORT_UNICODE` defined, `LINK_SIZE == 2`,\n8\t`IMM2_SIZE == 2`, **no** `SUPPORT_JIT`, no EBCDIC, no `PCRE2_DEBUG`,\n9\t`HAVE_BUILTIN_MUL_OVERFLOW` undefined, `HAVE_ATTRIBUTE_UNINITIALIZED` undefined.\n10\tSo: only translate the code that the C preprocessor keeps for that configuration.\n11\tCode inside `#ifdef SUPPORT_JIT`, `#ifdef EBCDIC`, `#ifdef PCRE2_DEBUG`,\n12\t`#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 16/32`, `#ifdef DEBUG_*` etc. must be **omitted**.\n13\tCode inside `#ifdef SUPPORT_UNICODE`, `#ifdef SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS`,\n14\t`#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 8`, `#ifndef SUPPORT_JIT`, `#ifndef EBCDIC` must be\n15\t**kept**.\n16\t\n17\t## Golden rules\n18\t\n19\t1. **Transliterate, do not redesign.** Keep the same control flow, the same order\n20\t   of tests, the same variable names, the same helper functions (as private Rust\n21\t   `unsafe fn`s), the same table contents. Reproduce C bugs exactly.\n22\t2. **No panics ever.** A panic aborts the process. Never use `.unwrap()` on\n23\t   `Option<fn>` unless C already dereferenced the pointer unconditionally; never\n24\t   index a Rust array/slice with a value that could be out of range - read through\n25\t   raw pointers instead (`*TABLE.as_ptr().add(i)`).\n26\t3. Everything is `unsafe`: write `unsafe fn` / `unsafe extern \"C\" fn` and use raw\n27\t   pointers exactly like the C code (`.add(n)`, `.offset(n)`, `.sub(n)`,\n28\t   `ptr1.offset_from(ptr2)` for pointer differences).\n29\t4. Integer types must match C: `int` -> `c_int` (= i32), `unsigned int` -> `c_uint`\n30\t   (u32), `uint32_t` -> u32, `PCRE2_SIZE`/`size_t` -> `usize`, `BOOL` -> `BOOL`\n31\t   (= i32, values `TRUE`/`FALSE`). Arithmetic wraps (release profile has\n32\t   `overflow-checks = false`).\n33\t5. Do **not** add `mod` statements: `src/lib.rs` already declares every module.\n34\t   Each module starts with:\n35\t   ```rust\n36\t   use crate::internal::*;\n37\t   ```\n38\t   (macros are exported at the crate root and are used as `GET!(...)`, `PUT!(...)`).\n39\t\n40\t## What is already available (read `src/internal.rs` + `src/macros.rs`)\n41\t\n42\t* Types: `PCRE2_UCHAR` (u8), `PCRE2_SPTR` (`*const u8`), `PCRE2_SIZE` (usize),\n43\t  `BOOL` (i32), `TRUE`, `FALSE`, `PCRE2_UNSET`, `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED`.\n44\t* All `#[repr(C)]` structures: `pcre2_memctl`, `pcre2_real_code`,\n45\t  `pcre2_real_match_data`, `pcre2_real_compile_context`, `pcre2_real_match_context`,\n46\t  `pcre2_real_convert_context`, `pcre2_real_general_context`, `compile_block`,\n47\t  `match_block`, `dfa_match_block`, `heapframe` (+ its `fields` union types\n48\t  `hf_char_repeat`, ...), `named_group`, `branch_chain`, `open_capitem`,\n49\t  `class_ranges`, `recurse_arguments`, `compile_data`, `class_bits_storage`,\n50\t  `ucd_record`, `ucp_type_table`, `pcre2_callout_block`,\n51\t  `pcre2_callout_enumerate_block`, `pcre2_substitute_callout_block`,\n52\t  `eclass_op_info`, `dfa_recursion_info`, `recurse_check`, `parsed_recurse_check`,\n53\t  `recurse_cache`, `pcre2_serialized_data`, `pcre2_real_jit_stack`.\n54\t* All constants: `PCRE2_*` (public + private flags), `OP_*` (u32), `ESC_*` (i32),\n55\t  `META_*` (u32), `ERR1..ERR120` (i32), `PT_*`, `XCL_*`, `ECL_*`, `cbit_*`,\n56\t  `ctype_*`, `lcc_offset`, `fcc_offset`, `cbits_offset`, `ctypes_offset`,\n57\t  `TABLES_LENGTH`, `CHAR_*` (u32, e.g. `CHAR_a`), `ucp_*` (u32),\n58\t  `MAGIC_NUMBER`, `LINK_SIZE`, `IMM2_SIZE`, `MAX_*`, `NLTYPE_*`, ...\n59\t* Data tables (already transcribed): `_pcre2_OP_lengths_8`, `_pcre2_hspace_list_8`,\n60\t  `_pcre2_vspace_list_8`, `_pcre2_callout_start_delims_8`,\n61\t  `_pcre2_callout_end_delims_8`, `_pcre2_utf8_table1..4`, `_pcre2_utf8_table1_size`,\n62\t  `_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8`, `_pcre2_ucp_gbtable_8`, `_pcre2_utt_8`,\n63\t  `_pcre2_utt_names_8`, `_pcre2_utt_size_8`, `_pcre2_default_tables_8`,\n64\t  `_pcre2_ucd_*`, `_pcre2_unicode_version_8`.\n65\t  In C these are referred to as `PRIV(name)`, e.g. `PRIV(OP_lengths)[x]` becomes\n66\t  `_pcre2_OP_lengths_8[x as usize]`.\n67\t* libc: `malloc`, `free`, `memcpy`, `memmove`, `memset`, `memcmp`, `memchr`,\n68\t  `strlen`, `strcmp`, `isspace`, `isdigit`, ... `tolower`, `toupper`\n69\t  (declared `extern \"C\"`, call them exactly as C does).\n70\t* **Every** library function (public `pcre2_xxx_8` and private `_pcre2_xxx_8`) is\n71\t  declared in an `extern \"C\"` block in `internal.rs`, so you can call any of them\n72\t  by its linker name without knowing which module defines it. In C these calls\n73\t  look like `PRIV(strlen)(x)` or `pcre2_match(...)`; write `_pcre2_strlen_8(x)` /\n74\t  `pcre2_match_8(...)`.\n75\t* UCD accessors are inline fns: `GET_UCD(c)`, `UCD_CHARTYPE(c)`, `UCD_SCRIPT(c)`,\n76\t  `UCD_CATEGORY(c)`, `UCD_GRAPHBREAK(c)`, `UCD_CASESET(c)`, `UCD_OTHERCASE(c)`,\n77\t  `UCD_SCRIPTX(c)`, `UCD_BPROPS(c)`, `UCD_BIDICLASS(c)`, `UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP(p)`,\n78\t  `UCD_BIDICLASS_PROP(p)`, `UCD_BPROPS_PROP(p)`, `UCD_ANY_I(c)`, `UCD_DOTTED_I(c)`,\n79\t  `UCD_FOLD_I_TURKISH(c)`.\n80\t* Macros (in `src/macros.rs`, called with `!`): `GET!`, `PUT!`, `GET2!`, `PUT2!`,\n81\t  `PUTINC!`, `PUT2INC!`, `GETCHAR!`, `GETCHARINC!`, `GETCHARLEN!`, `GETUTF8!`,\n82\t  `GETUTF8INC!`, `GETUTF8LEN!`, `BACKCHAR!`, `FORWARDCHAR!`, `FORWARDCHARTEST!`,\n83\t  `ACROSSCHAR!`, `MAPBIT!`, `MAPSET!`, `SETBIT!`, `TABLE_GET!`, `MAX_255!`,\n84\t  `CHMAX_255!`, `META_CODE!`, `META_DATA!`, `META_DIFF!`, `PUTOFFSET!`,\n85\t  `GETOFFSET!`, `GETPLUSOFFSET!`, `READPLUSOFFSET!`, `SKIPOFFSET!`, `CU2BYTES!`,\n86\t  `BYTES2CU!`, `CLIST_ALIGN_TO!`, `GET_MAX_CHAR_VALUE!`, `SELECT_VALUE8!`,\n87\t  `HAS_EXTRALEN!`, `GET_EXTRALEN!`, `NOT_FIRSTCU!`, `HASUTF8EXTRALEN!`, `PUTCHAR!`,\n88\t  `IS_NEWLINE!`, `WAS_NEWLINE!`.\n89\t  **Differences from C**: the macros whose C version implicitly used the local\n90\t  variable `utf` take it as an extra last argument:\n91\t  `GETCHARTEST!(c, eptr, utf)`, `GETCHARINCTEST!(c, eptr, utf)`,\n92\t  `GETCHARLENTEST!(c, eptr, len, utf)`, `PUTCHAR!(c, p, utf)`,\n93\t  `GET_MAX_CHAR_VALUE!(utf)`.\n94\t  `IS_NEWLINE!(p, blk, psend, utf)` / `WAS_NEWLINE!(p, blk, psstart, utf)` take the\n95\t  NLBLOCK pointer and the PSEND/PSSTART expression explicitly, e.g. the C\n96\t  `IS_NEWLINE(ptr)` inside pcre2_match.c (NLBLOCK = mb, PSEND = end_subject)\n97\t  becomes `IS_NEWLINE!(ptr, mb, (*mb).end_subject, utf)`.\n98\t\n99\t## Translation patterns\n100\t\n101\t| C | Rust |\n102\t|---|---|\n103\t| `PCRE2_SPTR p = ...; p++` | `let mut p: PCRE2_SPTR = ...; p = p.add(1);` |\n104\t| `*p++` | `{ let t = *p; p = p.add(1); t }` |\n105\t| `p[3]` | `*p.add(3)` |\n106\t| `p - q` (pointers) | `p.offset_from(q)` (i64) - cast as needed |\n107\t| `if (x)` where x is int | `if x != 0` |\n108\t| `if (ptr == NULL)` | `if ptr.is_null()` |\n109\t| `NULL` | `std::ptr::null_mut()` / `std::ptr::null()` |\n110\t| `(void)x;` | omit |\n111\t| `sizeof(T)` | `size_of::<T>()` |\n112\t| `offsetof(S, f)` | `offset_of!(S, f)` |\n113\t| `switch (x) { case A: ... }` | `match x { A => {...}, _ => {} }` - but if the C code falls through or uses `break` to leave the switch inside a loop, use `if/else if` chains or a labeled block; **never** change semantics |\n114\t| `for (;;) { ... }` | `loop { ... }` |\n115\t| `do {...} while (c)` | `loop { ... if !(c) { break } }` |\n116\t| `goto LABEL;` forward | wrap the region in `'label: { ... break 'label; ... }` |\n117\t| `goto LABEL;` backward | `'label: loop { ... continue 'label; ... break; }` |\n118\t| `x = TRUE` (BOOL) | `x = TRUE` |\n119\t| struct field `->` | `(*ptr).field` |\n120\t| callbacks (`Option<fn>`) | `if (*mcontext).callout.is_some() { ((*mcontext).callout.unwrap())(args) }` |\n121\t| char literal `'a'` | `CHAR_a` (u32) - cast with `as u8` when storing a code unit |\n122\t| `\"literal\"` | `b\"literal\\0\"` (keep the NUL when C relies on it) |\n123\t\n124\tComparisons between a code unit (u8) and a `CHAR_*` constant (u32): write\n125\t`*p as u32 == CHAR_a` or `*p == CHAR_a as u8` - pick one and be consistent.\n126\t\n127\tLocal `static const` tables inside a C file become private module-level statics:\n128\t`static tablename: [u8; N] = [...];` (exact same values, same order).\n129\t\n130\t## Exported symbols\n131\t\n132\tFor every function that the C library exports (the `nm -D` list), the Rust\n133\tdefinition must be:\n134\t\n135\t```rust\n136\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n137\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn pcre2_compile_8(...) -> *mut pcre2_real_code { ... }\n138\t```\n139\t\n140\tThe linker name must match **exactly** what the C macros produce (e.g.\n141\t`_pcre2_compile_add_name_to_table8` has no underscore before the `8`, but\n142\t`_pcre2_compile_class_nested_8` does). Your task description gives you the exact\n143\tnames to define. Private (`static`) C functions must NOT be `no_mangle` and must\n144\tNOT be `pub`.\n145\t\n146\t## Style / hygiene\n147\t\n148\t* Keep the C comments (they explain the tricky bits) - copy the important ones.\n149\t* Do not reformat the logic into \"nicer\" Rust: no iterators, no `Option<>`\n150\t  wrapping, no bounds-checked slices in hot paths.\n151\t* Do not use any external crate. `std` is available.\n152\t* Do not modify `c_src/`, `Cargo.toml`, `src/lib.rs`, `src/internal.rs`,\n153\t  `src/macros.rs`, or any file that is not yours.\n154\t* When you need a helper that C got from a macro that is not listed above,\n155\t  write it as a private `#[inline] unsafe fn` in your module.\n156\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0194jx7XYGxHvgm4sUhy7TVo","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc","uuid":"4c18e4f3-f259-4546-8c