s built from the STR_x macros, and the code\nindexes into them with offsets computed from the item tables, so they must be\nbyte-for-byte identical. Write them as `static verbnames: [u8; N] = *b\"\\0MARK\\0ACCEPT\\0...\";`\nstyle literals (work out the exact bytes; each C `STRING_xxx0` macro ends with an\nexplicit NUL, and the C compiler adds one more NUL at the very end of the whole\nconcatenated literal - be careful to reproduce that). Where the C table entries\nare `{ n, m }` style struct initializers, translate them as Rust struct literals\nwith the same field values (compute any `sizeof`/macro arithmetic by hand).\nFor `pso_list`, the C entries use string literals and lengths - reproduce exactly.\n\nDouble-check your tables by counting entries and comparing with the C source (you\nmay write a throw-away script in $TMPDIR to compare, e.g. by compiling the C\ntable into a tiny C program and dumping the bytes; do NOT add files to the repo).\n\nFIDELITY IS EVERYTHING.\n\nReport the items you defined (with their lengths) and the exact output of the verification command from the guide."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2789,"cache_read_input_tokens":570889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2789,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc","uuid":"2bd6fd54-4291-4716-a94f-2c46b8b45885","timestamp":"2026-08-22T22:39:46.572Z"}
