erified the arithmetic maps each `*I` opcode onto its caseful twin (e.g. `OP_NOTPOSUPTOI` 84 - 13 = 71 = `OP_NOTPOSUPTO`).\n- Per-arm order preserved: PLUS does `count = (*current_state).count` then conditional `ADD_ACTIVE!(state_offset + dlen + 1, 0)`; QUERY/STAR do unconditional `ADD_ACTIVE!(state_offset + dlen + 1, 0)`; EXACT has no `ADD_ACTIVE` and no possessive removal; UPTO does `ADD_ACTIVE!(state_offset + dlen + 1 + IMM2_SIZE, 0)` before reading `count`.\n- `otherd` initialised to `NOTACHAR`, then `UCD_OTHERCASE(d)` when `utf_or_ucp != 0 && d >= 128`, else `TABLE_GET!(d, fcc, d) as u32` (checked `pcre2_intmodedep.h:234` — the 8-bit `TABLE_GET` is a plain `(table)[c]`, matching the Rust macro's unchecked pointer offset, so no bounds panic).\n- `(c == d || c == otherd) == (codevalue < OP_NOTSTAR)` kept as a direct bool-equality comparison.\n- Possessive \"remove non-match possibility\" is `active_count -= 1; next_active_state = next_active_state.sub(1);`.\n- `++count >= (int)GET2(code, 1)` became `count += 1; if count >= GET2!(code, 1) as c_int`, with `ADD_NEW!(state_offset + dlen + 1 + IMM2_SIZE as c_int, 0)` / `ADD_NEW!(state_offset, count)`.\n- Every arm ends with `break 'next_active_state;`. No bug fixes, no reordering.\n\n## Verification\n\nCommand: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-ZSaIwY/translated_rust && cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A15 | head -80`\n\nExact output: (empty — no errors)\n\nFull build finishes with only pre-existing warnings unrelated to my file (`unused import: crate::internal::*` in placeholder modules, `unused macro definition: ADD_ACTIVE_DATA` in the skeleton). No diagnostic anywhere points at `pcre2_dfa_ops5.rs`. Note: one transient error from a concurrent agent (`couldn't read src/pcre2_compile_tables.rs`) appeared mid-run and resolved itself; it was not in my file.","usage":{"total_tokens":62092,"tool_uses":24,"duration_ms":252917},"uuid":"3840f781-3e57-49ec-81bf-ebc1a7ef6620","session_id"