{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SbeVt21vi3PBSsxhXc47o7","type":"tool_result","content":"1000\tcharacters to a class. The list must be in order so that ranges of characters\n1001\tcan be detected and handled appropriately. This function sets the overall range\n1002\tso that the internal functions can try to avoid duplication when handling\n1003\tcase-independence.\n1004\t\n1005\tArguments:\n1006\t  options       the options bits\n1007\t  xoptions      the extra options bits\n1008\t  cb            contains pointers to tables etc.\n1009\t  p             points to row of 32-bit values, terminated by NOTACHAR\n1010\t\n1011\tReturns:        cb->classbits is updated\n1012\t*/\n1013\t\n1014\tstatic void\n1015\tadd_list_to_class(uint32_t options, uint32_t xoptions, compile_block *cb,\n1016\t  const uint32_t *p)\n1017\t{\n1018\twhile (p[0] < 256)\n1019\t  {\n1020\t  unsigned int n = 0;\n1021\t\n1022\t  while(p[n+1] == p[0] + n + 1) n++;\n1023\t  add_to_class(options, xoptions, cb, p[0], p[n]);\n1024\t\n1025\t  p += n + 1;\n1026\t  }\n1027\t}\n1028\t\n1029\t\n1030\t\n1031\t/*************************************************\n1032\t*    Add characters not in a list to a class     *\n1033\t*************************************************/\n1034\t\n1035\t/* This function is used for adding the complement of a list of horizontal or\n1036\tvertical whitespace to a class. The list must be in order.\n1037\t\n1038\tArguments:\n1039\t  options       the options bits\n1040\t  xoptions      the extra options bits\n1041\t  cb            contains pointers to tables etc.\n1042\t  p             points to row of 32-bit values, terminated by NOTACHAR\n1043\t\n1044\tReturns:        cb->classbits is updated\n1045\t*/\n1046\t\n1047\tstatic void\n1048\tadd_not_list_to_class(uint32_t options, uint32_t xoptions, compile_block *cb,\n1049\t  const uint32_t *p)\n1050\t{\n1051\tif (p[0] > 0)\n1052\t  add_to_class(options, xoptions, cb, 0, p[0] - 1);\n1053\