{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01J2awaWpcwFXTjageSyDdX1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Translated from c_src/src/pcre2_find_bracket.c\n2\tuse crate::internal::*;\n3\t\n4\t/* This module contains a single function that scans through a compiled pattern\n5\tuntil it finds a capturing bracket with the given number, or, if the number is\n6\tnegative, an instance of OP_REVERSE or OP_VREVERSE for a lookbehind. The\n7\tfunction is called from pcre2_compile.c and also from pcre2_study.c when\n8\tfinding the minimum matching length. */\n9\t\n10\t/*************************************************\n11\t*    Scan compiled regex for specific bracket    *\n12\t*************************************************/\n13\t\n14\t/*\n15\tArguments:\n16\t  code        points to start of expression\n17\t  utf         TRUE in UTF mode\n18\t  number      the required bracket number or negative to find a lookbehind\n19\t\n20\tReturns:      pointer to the opcode for the bracket, or NULL if not found\n21\t*/\n22\t\n23\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n24\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _pcre2_find_bracket_8(\n25\t    code: PCRE2_SPTR,\n26\t    utf: BOOL,\n27\t    number: c_int,\n28\t) -> PCRE2_SPTR {\n29\t    let mut code: PCRE2_SPTR = code;\n30\t\n31\t    loop {\n32\t        let c: PCRE2_UCHAR = *code;\n33\t\n34\t        if c as u32 == OP_END {\n35\t            return std::ptr::null();\n36\t        }\n37\t\n38\t        /* XCLASS is used for classes that cannot be represented just by a bit map.\n39\t        This includes negated single high-valued characters. ECLASS is used for\n40\t        classes that use set operations internally. CALLOUT_STR is used for\n41\t        callouts with string arguments. In each case the length in the table is\n42\t        zero; the actual length is stored in the compiled code. */\n43\t\n44\t        if c as u32 == OP_XCLASS || c as u32 == OP_ECLASS {\n45\t            code = code.add(GET!(code, 1) as usize);\n46\t        } else