e, tcode.add(1), FALSE, utf, ucp)`.\n- Preserved the C bug in `set_type_bits`: the high-byte loop tests `re->tables[cbits_offset + c/8]` **without** adding `cbit_type` — reproduced verbatim.\n- `study_char_list` reads its `uint16_t`/`uint32_t` items via `std::ptr::read_unaligned` (same bytes, no UB risk), and the byte-wide `start` loop counters use `wrapping_add` so no overflow panic is possible.\n- Only the 8-bit / `SUPPORT_UNICODE` branches were kept; the `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH != 8` alternatives and `(void)utf;` casts were dropped.\n\n## Final verification output\n\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A15 | head -80` reports 7 errors, none in my file: `SSB_UNKNOWN`, `SSB_DONE`, `MAX_CACHE_BACKREF` (part 1 still a placeholder), `set_start_bits` and `find_minlength` (part 3 still a placeholder) — all spans in `src/pcre2_study_p4.rs` — plus unrelated errors in `src/pcre2_compile_p7.rs` (`compile_branch`) and `src/pcre2_compile_class_p4.rs` (a `bool`/`BOOL` mismatch at line 310). `pcre2_study_p2.rs` appears in the output only as a rustc \"a function with a similar name exists\" hint for `set_type_bits`.","usage":{"total_tokens":59616,"tool_uses":27,"duration_ms":227569},"uuid":"f09e3c35-f73e-4d26-bc69-1b2e6bee91d6","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc"}
