{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01HR2jynfutbPzwkfovsqhad","type":"tool_result","content":"228\t}\n229\t\n230\t/*************************************************\n231\t*        Find length of a parsed branch          *\n232\t*************************************************/\n233\t\n234\t/* Return fixed maximum and minimum lengths for a branch in a lookbehind,\n235\tgiving an error if the length is not limited. On entry, *pptrptr points to the\n236\tfirst element inside the branch. On exit it is set to point to the ALT or KET.\n237\t\n238\tArguments:\n239\t  pptrptr     pointer to pointer in the parsed pattern\n240\t  minptr      where to return the minimum length\n241\t  errcodeptr  pointer to error code\n242\t  lcptr       pointer to loop counter\n243\t  recurses    chain of recurse_check to catch mutual recursion\n244\t  cb          pointer to compile block\n245\t\n246\tReturns:      the maximum length, or a negative value on error\n247\t*/\n248\t\n249\tunsafe fn get_branchlength(\n250\t    pptrptr: *mut *mut u32,\n251\t    minptr: *mut c_int,\n252\t    errcodeptr: *mut c_int,\n253\t    lcptr: *mut c_int,\n254\t    recurses: *mut parsed_recurse_check,\n255\t    cb: *mut compile_block,\n256\t) -> c_int {\n257\t    let mut branchlength: c_int = 0;\n258\t    let mut branchminlength: c_int = 0;\n259\t    let mut grouplength: c_int;\n260\t    let mut groupminlength: c_int = 0;\n261\t    let mut lastitemlength: u32 = 0;\n262\t    let mut lastitemminlength: u32 = 0;\n263\t    let mut pptr: *mut u32 = *pptrptr;\n264\t    let mut offset: PCRE2_SIZE = 0;\n265\t    let mut this_recurse: parsed_recurse_check = parsed_recurse_check {\n266\t        prev: std::ptr::null_mut(),\n267\t        groupptr: std::ptr::null_mut(),\n268\t    };\n269\t\n270\t    /* A large and/or complex regex can take too long to process. This can happen\n271\t    more often when (?| groups are present in the pattern because their length\n272\t    cannot be ca