ectly as an array length); the C comparison `ptrstackptr >= PTR_STACK_SIZE` needs `PTR_STACK_SIZE as u32`.\n\nTranslation details: the C `for (;;ptr++)` loop in `find_text_end` uses a `'CONTINUE: { }` inner block so the C `continue` still runs the increment; `goto EXIT` / `goto FAILED` are labelled blocks. The `switch (erc)` and `switch (state->to_case)` became `if/else` chains with the C `default` arm last. `errorcode`/`ch` are zero-initialized (C leaves them uninitialized but `check_escape` always writes `*errorcodeptr`). `PCRE2_ASSERT`/`PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE` are no-ops (the latter's `return 0;` is kept). No bugs fixed; `MAX_255!` still expands to `TRUE` as in 8-bit C.\n\n## Verification output\n\n`cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A15 | head -80` reports 7 errors, **none in my file**: 6× `E0428 ... defined multiple times` at `src/pcre2_auto_possess_p2.rs:661-668` (stub duplicates of `autoposstab`, `propposstab`, `catposstab`, `posspropstab`, `check_char_prop`, colliding with `pcre2_auto_possess_p1.rs`) and 1 error at `src/pcre2_compile_parse_regex.rs:2091:77` — all other agents' in-progress files.\n\nBecause the crate does not currently link, I additionally verified my file in isolation: I copied the crate to `$TMPDIR`, blanked only the then-syntactically-broken `pcre2_compile_parse_regex.rs`, and built — zero diagnostics referencing `pcre2_substitute_p1.rs`. I confirmed the module really was type-checked (not skipped) by injecting a deliberate type error into the temp copy and seeing it reported, then discarded the temp tree.","usage":{"total_tokens":79423,"tool_uses":36,"duration_ms":467896},"uuid":"2f81dacc-0dc3-456c-b07f-785ac33652eb","session_id":"69c7dc4d-05f2-4bba-997b-e68ff82cc8bc"}
