ted between arms). C quirks preserved: depth is never decremented; `u8` range loop uses `wrapping_add` so it can never panic.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe exact command in the project dir currently fails on **other agents' in-progress files only** — 7 errors, spans in `src/pcre2_auto_possess_p2.rs:661-668` (`autoposstab`, `propposstab`, `catposstab`, `posspropstab`, `check_char_prop`, `get_chr_property_list` \"defined multiple times\" against the real definitions in `_p1.rs`) and `src/pcre2_compile_parse_regex.rs:2091` (\"this file contains an unclosed delimiter\"). `grep -c pcre2_study_p3` over the full error output = **0**.\n\nBecause a parse error in another file aborts the whole crate, I also built an isolated copy in `$TMPDIR/verify` (full tree, only the mid-write `pcre2_compile_parse_regex.rs` stubbed out). Exact output of `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A15 | head -80` there:\n\n```\nerror[E0425]: cannot find function `parse_regex` in this scope\n   --> src/pcre2_compile_p10.rs:523:33\n    |\n523 |                     errorcode = parse_regex(\n    |                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^ not found in this scope\n\nFor more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0425`.\nwarning: `pcre2` (lib) generated 2 warnings\nerror: could not compile `pcre2` (lib) due to 1 previous error; 2 warnings emitted\n```\n\ni.e. the entire crate (including `pcre2_study`) compiles; the only error is the function from the file I stubbed. The 2 warnings are pre-existing and in other files (`pcre2_chartables.rs` unused import, `pcre2_dfa_match.rs` unused macro). My file produces zero errors and zero warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":644,"cache_read_input_tokens":139826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":644,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Eg8LZ