{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016Sq5D8FXHxbNUBc9TYjmxb","type":"tool_result","content":"347\t/* Non-empty character class. If the included characters are all < 256, we\n348\tbuild a 32-byte bitmap of the permitted characters, except in the special\n349\tcase where there is only one such character. For negated classes, we build\n350\tthe map as usual, then invert it at the end. However, we use a different\n351\topcode so that data characters > 255 can be handled correctly.\n352\t\n353\tIf the class contains characters outside the 0-255 range, a different\n354\topcode is compiled. It may optionally have a bit map for characters < 256,\n355\tbut those above are explicitly listed afterwards. A flag code unit tells\n356\twhether the bitmap is present, and whether this is a negated class or\n357\tnot. */\n358\telse if meta == META_CLASS_NOT || meta == META_CLASS {\n359\t    matched_char = TRUE;\n360\t\n361\t    /* Check for complex extended classes and handle them separately. */\n362\t\n363\t    if (*pptr & CLASS_IS_ECLASS) != 0 {\n364\t        if _pcre2_compile_class_nested_8(\n365\t            options,\n366\t            xoptions,\n367\t            &mut pptr,\n368\t            &mut code,\n369\t            errorcodeptr,\n370\t            cb,\n371\t            lengthptr,\n372\t        ) == 0\n373\t        {\n374\t            return 0;\n375\t        }\n376\t        break 'class_end_processing;\n377\t    }\n378\t\n379\t    /* We can optimize the case of a single character in a class by generating\n380\t    OP_CHAR or OP_CHARI if it's positive, or OP_NOT or OP_NOTI if it's\n381\t    negative. In the negative case there can be no first char if this item is\n382\t    first, whatever repeat count may follow. In the case of reqcu, save the\n383\t    previous value for reinstating. */\n384\t\n385\t    if *pptr.add(1) < META_END && *pptr.add(2) == META_CLASS_END {\n386\t        let c: u32 = *pptr.add(1);\n387\t\n388\t        pptr = pp